/-!
# Stacks 053R for integral schemes, from the affine case

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a dominant morphism locally of finite type between *integral* schemes and let
`I` be a locally principal ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme misses the generic fibre. At
a point `s` of `S` whose fibre has dimension at most that of the generic fibre, the support of `I`
inside the fibre `X_s` is a union of irreducible components of `X_s`.

This file is the scheme-level glue of that statement: it reduces it to the affine statement about
a finite type extension `A → B` of domains and a single element `g` of `B`, which enters here as
an explicit hypothesis `haffine`. The reduction has two steps.

The first step is the chart step. A point of the support inside `X_s` has an affine open
neighbourhood `U` on which `I` is principal, say generated by `g ∈ Γ(X, U)`, and small enough to
be carried by `f` into an affine open `V` containing `s`. Then `Spec Γ(X, U) ⟶ Spec Γ(S, V)` is
the map on spectra of a finite type extension of domains — of *domains* because `X` and `S` are
integral, and injective because the morphism of spectra is dominant and `Γ(S, V)` is reduced —
and its base change to the generic point is the generic fibre of `f`, so both the emptiness
hypothesis and the dimension hypothesis descend to it. The support of `I` on the chart is the
zero locus of `g`, so `haffine` applies verbatim.

The second step is to glue the charts, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.fiber_preimage_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_openCharts`: the shape
"a closed set is the union of the ambient irreducible components it contains" is local on the
fibre, so it suffices to know it on a family of open subschemes of `X` covering the support
inside `X_s`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_eq_topologicalKrullDimAt`: the generic
  fibre of a dominant morphism locally of finite type between irreducible schemes is irreducible
  of pure dimension, so its dimension is its local dimension at any one of its points.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_comp_eq_of_isOpenImmersion`:
  restricting the source along an open immersion with irreducible source does not change the
  dimension of the generic fibre.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isUnit_algebraMap_fiber_bot`: an element of `B` lying in no prime of `B` that
  contracts to the zero ideal of the domain `A` becomes a unit in the generic fibre
  `Frac A ⊗[A] B`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_affineChart`: **the chart step of Stacks 053R.** On an
  affine open of `X` mapping into an affine open of `S` and on which `I` is principal, the
  conclusion of Stacks 053R follows from the affine statement.
* `Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents_integral`: **Stacks 053R for
  integral source and target,** granted the affine statement.
* `Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents_general`: **Stacks 053R**, with
  no Noetherian hypothesis — the affine statement discharged by the descent of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.AffineDescent`, and integrality obtained from
  irreducibility by the reduction step of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.IntegralReduction`.

## Implementation notes

The affine statement is taken as the hypothesis `haffine` rather than imported, so that this file
can be read and checked independently of its proof. Its generic-fibre hypothesis is phrased as
`IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g)`, which under the local instance
`Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra` is the unit `1 ⊗ₜ g` of `Frac A ⊗[A] B`; its injectivity
hypothesis is packaged as `FaithfulSMul A B`.

`Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_affineChart` takes the base point as a point `s` of `S`
together with a proof that it lies in the chosen affine open of `S`, and produces the
corresponding prime of `Γ(S, V)` from `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.range_fromSpec` rather than
from the isomorphism `V ≅ Spec Γ(S, V)`; this avoids having to identify a round trip through that
isomorphism with the identity.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 053R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/053R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A21](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A21)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### The dimension of the generic fibre -/

/-- The generic fibre of a dominant morphism locally of finite type between irreducible schemes
has the same dimension as its local dimension at any one of its points: it is irreducible,
because the generic point of the source lies in it and specializes to all of its points, and it
is locally of finite type over the residue field at the generic point of the target, so Stacks
0A21 applies. -/
public theorem topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_eq_topologicalKrullDimAt {X S : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ S) [IrreducibleSpace X] [IrreducibleSpace S] [IsDominant f]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (x : f.fiber (genericPoint S)) :
    topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber (genericPoint S)) =
      topologicalKrullDimAt (f.fiber (genericPoint S)) x := by
  have : IrreducibleSpace (f.fiber (genericPoint S)) := by
    rw [← apply_genericPoint_eq_genericPoint f]
    exact irreducibleSpace_fiber_apply_genericPoint f
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (f.fiberToSpecResidueField (genericPoint S)) :=
    (inferInstance : LocallyOfFiniteType
      (Limits.pullback.snd f (S.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint S))))
  exact topologicalKrullDim_eq_topologicalKrullDimAt_of_irreducible
    (S.residueField (genericPoint S)) _ (f.fiberToSpecResidueField (genericPoint S)) x

/-- A morphism from an irreducible scheme sending the generic point to the generic point of an
irreducible target is dominant. -/
private theorem isDominant_of_apply_genericPoint_eq {X S : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace X]
    [IrreducibleSpace S] (f : X ⟶ S) (h : f (genericPoint X) = genericPoint S) : IsDominant f := by
  refine ⟨denseRange_iff_closure_range.mpr (Set.eq_univ_of_univ_subset ?_)⟩
  rw [← genericPoint_spec S]
  exact closure_mono (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr ⟨genericPoint X, h⟩)

/-- Restricting the source of a dominant morphism locally of finite type between irreducible
schemes along an open immersion with irreducible source leaves the dimension of the generic fibre
unchanged: both are local dimensions at corresponding points of the two generic fibres, and the
comparison map of fibres is an open embedding. -/
public theorem topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_comp_eq_of_isOpenImmersion
    {X Y S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (i : Y ⟶ X) [IrreducibleSpace X] [IrreducibleSpace Y]
    [IrreducibleSpace S] [IsDominant f] [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [IsOpenImmersion i] :
    topologicalKrullDim ((i ≫ f).fiber (genericPoint S)) =
      topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber (genericPoint S)) := by
  have hgen : (i ≫ f) (genericPoint Y) = genericPoint S := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, genericPoint_eq_of_isOpenImmersion,
      apply_genericPoint_eq_genericPoint]
  have : IsDominant (i ≫ f) := isDominant_of_apply_genericPoint_eq _ hgen
  have hpoint : ((i ≫ f).fiber (genericPoint S)) :=
    ((i ≫ f).fiberHomeo (genericPoint S)).symm
      ⟨genericPoint Y, apply_genericPoint_eq_genericPoint (i ≫ f)⟩
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_eq_topologicalKrullDimAt (i ≫ f) hpoint,
    topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_eq_topologicalKrullDimAt f
      (f.fiberMap i (genericPoint S) hpoint)]
  exact ((f.fiberMap i (genericPoint S)).isOpenEmbedding.topologicalKrullDimAt_eq hpoint).symm

/-! ### Units in the generic fibre of an affine morphism -/

/-- An element `g` of an `A`-algebra `B`, for `A` a domain, becomes a unit of the generic fibre
`(⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B = Frac A ⊗[A] B` as soon as no prime of `B` containing `g`
contracts to the zero ideal of `A`: the primes of the generic fibre are exactly the primes of `B`
contracting to the zero ideal, so the zero locus of `g` there is empty. -/
public theorem isUnit_algebraMap_fiber_bot {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A]
    [Algebra A B] (g : B)
    (hgeneric : ∀ q : PrimeSpectrum B, g ∈ q.asIdeal →
      PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap A B) q ≠ (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A)) :
    IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g) := by
  apply Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top.mp
  apply PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_empty_iff_eq_top.mp
  rw [PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_span]
  refine Set.eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem.mpr fun q hq => ?_
  have hmem : algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g ∈ q.asIdeal :=
    hq (Set.mem_singleton _)
  set point := (PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber A B (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A)).symm q with hpoint
  refine hgeneric point.1 ?_ point.2
  exact hmem

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Stacks.Divisors

open AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **The chart step of Stacks 053R.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a dominant morphism locally of finite
type between integral schemes, `I` an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme misses the generic
fibre, and `s` a point of `S` whose fibre has dimension at most that of the generic fibre. Let
`U ⊆ X` be a nonempty affine open on which `I` is principal, mapping into an affine open `V ⊆ S`
containing `s`. Then, inside the fibre over `s` of the restriction `Spec Γ(X, U) ⟶ S` of `f`, the
part lying in the support of `I` is a union of irreducible components.

This is the affine statement `haffine` applied to the finite type extension of domains
`Γ(S, V) → Γ(X, U)`: the extension is injective because `Spec Γ(X, U) ⟶ Spec Γ(S, V)` is dominant
and `Γ(S, V)` is reduced, the generator of `I` on `U` becomes a unit in the generic fibre because
the closed subscheme misses the generic fibre of `f`, and the two dimension hypotheses match
because `V ⟶ S` and `U ⟶ X` are open immersions. -/
public theorem fiber_support_eq_union_affineChart {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) [IsIntegral X]
    [IsIntegral S] [IsDominant f] [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (haffine : ∀ (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B]
      [Algebra A B] [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] (g : B) (p : PrimeSpectrum A),
      IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g) →
      topologicalKrullDim ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) ≤
        topologicalKrullDim ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber
          (genericPoint (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)))) →
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι p ⁻¹'
          (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} : Set (PrimeSpectrum B)) =
        ⋃₀ {C : Set ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) |
          C ∈ irreducibleComponents ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) ∧
          C ⊆ (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι p ⁻¹'
            (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} : Set (PrimeSpectrum B))})
    (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hgeneric : IsEmpty ((I.subschemeι ≫ f).fiber (genericPoint S))) (s : S)
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber s) ≤ topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber (genericPoint S)))
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {V : S.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V) [Nonempty U]
    (hs : s ∈ V) (hsubset : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V)
    (hprincipal : (I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩).IsPrincipal) :
    (hU.fromSpec ≫ f).fiberι s ⁻¹' (hU.fromSpec.base ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X)) =
      ⋃₀ {C : Set ((hU.fromSpec ≫ f).fiber s) |
        C ∈ irreducibleComponents ((hU.fromSpec ≫ f).fiber s) ∧
        C ⊆ (hU.fromSpec ≫ f).fiberι s ⁻¹' (hU.fromSpec.base ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X))} := by
  have : Nonempty V := ⟨⟨s, hs⟩⟩
  have : IsDomain Γ(X, U) := IsIntegral.component_integral U
  have : IsDomain Γ(S, V) := IsIntegral.component_integral V
  let : Algebra Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U) := (f.appLE V U hsubset).hom.toAlgebra
  set morphism := Spec.map (f.appLE V U hsubset) with hmorphism
  -- The chart square.
  have hnat : morphism ≫ hV.fromSpec = hU.fromSpec ≫ f := hV.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec f hU hsubset
  -- A prime of `Γ(S, V)` above `s`.
  obtain ⟨basePrime, hbasePrime⟩ : ∃ p, hV.fromSpec p = s := by
    have hrange : s ∈ Set.range hV.fromSpec.base := by
      rw [hV.range_fromSpec]
      exact hs
    exact hrange
  -- The chart morphism is dominant, since it matches the generic points.
  have hgenericMap : morphism (genericPoint (Spec Γ(X, U))) = genericPoint (Spec Γ(S, V)) := by
    apply hV.fromSpec.isEmbedding.injective
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply morphism hV.fromSpec, hnat,
      Scheme.Hom.comp_apply hU.fromSpec f, genericPoint_eq_of_isOpenImmersion,
      apply_genericPoint_eq_genericPoint, genericPoint_eq_of_isOpenImmersion]
  have hdominant : IsDominant morphism := isDominant_of_apply_genericPoint_eq _ hgenericMap
  -- The chart extension is a finite type extension of domains, and it is injective.
  have hfinite : Algebra.FiniteType Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U) := f.finiteType_appLE hV hU hsubset
  have hinjective : Function.Injective (algebraMap Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U)) := by
    have hdense : DenseRange (PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U))) :=
      morphism.denseRange
    have hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U)) ≤ nilradical Γ(S, V) :=
      (PrimeSpectrum.denseRange_comap_iff_ker_le_nilRadical _).mp hdense
    rw [nilradical_eq_bot_iff.mpr (inferInstance : _root_.IsReduced Γ(S, V))] at hker
    exact (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mpr (le_bot_iff.mp hker)
  have hfaithful : FaithfulSMul Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U) :=
    (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective _ _).mpr hinjective
  -- The support of `I` on the chart is the zero locus of the generator.
  obtain ⟨element, helement⟩ := hprincipal
  have hsupport : hU.fromSpec.base ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X) =
      (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {element} : Set (PrimeSpectrum Γ(X, U))) := by
    have hequal : hU.fromSpec.base ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X) =
        hU.fromSpec.base ⁻¹' X.zeroLocus (U := U) (I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ : Set Γ(X, U)) := by
      ext p
      exact Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem (U := ⟨U, hU⟩)
        (hU.range_fromSpec.le ⟨p, rfl⟩)
    rw [hequal, hU.fromSpec_preimage_zeroLocus, helement, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_span]
  -- The generator is a unit in the generic fibre of the chart extension.
  have hunit : IsUnit (algebraMap Γ(X, U)
      ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum Γ(S, V)).asIdeal.Fiber Γ(X, U)) element) := by
    refine isUnit_algebraMap_fiber_bot (A := Γ(S, V)) (B := Γ(X, U)) element
      fun q hmem heq => ?_
    have hmemSupport : hU.fromSpec q ∈ (I.support : Set X) :=
      (Set.ext_iff.mp hsupport q).mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hmem)
    have heq' : morphism q = genericPoint (Spec Γ(S, V)) := by
      rw [genericPoint_eq_bot_of_affine]
      exact heq
    have hstep : (hU.fromSpec ≫ f) q = (morphism ≫ hV.fromSpec) q :=
      congrArg (fun m : Spec Γ(X, U) ⟶ S => m q) hnat.symm
    have hfgen : f (hU.fromSpec q) = genericPoint S :=
      (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply hU.fromSpec f q).symm.trans
        (hstep.trans ((Scheme.Hom.comp_apply morphism hV.fromSpec q).trans
          ((congrArg (fun z => hV.fromSpec z) heq').trans
            (genericPoint_eq_of_isOpenImmersion hV.fromSpec))))
    exact (I.isEmpty_fiber_comp_iff f (genericPoint S)).mp hgeneric _ hmemSupport hfgen
  -- The dimension hypothesis descends to the chart.
  have hdimension : topologicalKrullDim (morphism.fiber basePrime) ≤
      topologicalKrullDim (morphism.fiber (genericPoint (Spec Γ(S, V)))) := by
    have hleft := (fiberCompHomeo morphism hV.fromSpec
      basePrime).isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq
    have hright := (fiberCompHomeo morphism hV.fromSpec
      (genericPoint (Spec Γ(S, V)))).isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq
    rw [hnat, hbasePrime] at hleft
    rw [hnat, genericPoint_eq_of_isOpenImmersion] at hright
    rw [hleft, hright,
      topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_comp_eq_of_isOpenImmersion f hU.fromSpec]
    exact (f.fiberMap hU.fromSpec s).isEmbedding.isInducing.topologicalKrullDim_le.trans hdim
  -- The affine statement, read on the chart.
  have hcomponents : morphism.fiberι basePrime ⁻¹' (hU.fromSpec.base ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X)) =
      ⋃₀ {C : Set (morphism.fiber basePrime) |
        C ∈ irreducibleComponents (morphism.fiber basePrime) ∧
        C ⊆ morphism.fiberι basePrime ⁻¹' (hU.fromSpec.base ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X))} := by
    rw [hsupport, hmorphism]
    exact haffine Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U) element basePrime hunit hdimension
  have hresult := eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_fiber_comp morphism hV.fromSpec basePrime
    (hU.fromSpec.base ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X))
    (I.support.isClosed.preimage hU.fromSpec.continuous) hcomponents
  rwa [hnat, hbasePrime] at hresult

/-- **Stacks 053R for integral source and target,** granted the affine statement `haffine`. Let
`f : X ⟶ S` be a dominant morphism locally of finite type between integral schemes and let `I` be
a locally principal ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme misses the generic fibre. At a point
`s` of `S` whose fibre has dimension at most that of the generic fibre, the part of the fibre
`X_s` lying in the support of `I` is a union of irreducible components of `X_s`.

The statement is local on the fibre, so it suffices to check it on affine opens of `X` covering
the support inside `X_s`, which is `Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_affineChart`: around
each point of the support one picks an affine open on which `I` is principal and which `f` carries
into an affine open neighbourhood of `s`. -/
public theorem fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents_integral {X S : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ S) [IsIntegral X] [IsIntegral S] [IsDominant f] [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (haffine : ∀ (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B]
      [Algebra A B] [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] (g : B) (p : PrimeSpectrum A),
      IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g) →
      topologicalKrullDim ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) ≤
        topologicalKrullDim ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber
          (genericPoint (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)))) →
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι p ⁻¹'
          (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} : Set (PrimeSpectrum B)) =
        ⋃₀ {C : Set ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) |
          C ∈ irreducibleComponents ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) ∧
          C ⊆ (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι p ⁻¹'
            (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} : Set (PrimeSpectrum B))})
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (hI : IsLocallyPrincipal I)
    (hgeneric : IsEmpty ((I.subschemeι ≫ f).fiber (genericPoint S))) (s : S)
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber s) ≤ topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber (genericPoint S))) :
    (f.fiberι s) ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X) =
      ⋃₀ {C : Set (f.fiber s) | C ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber s) ∧
        C ⊆ (f.fiberι s) ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X)} := by
  refine fiber_preimage_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_openCharts f I s fun x hx => ?_
  have hambient : f (f.fiberι s x) = s := (f.range_fiberι s).le ⟨x, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hmemV, -⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (show s ∈ (⊤ : S.Opens) from trivial)
  obtain ⟨W, hmemW, hprincipalW⟩ := hI (f.fiberι s x)
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hmemU, hsubset⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset
      (show f.fiberι s x ∈ W.1 ⊓ f ⁻¹ᵁ V from
        ⟨hmemW, by change f (f.fiberι s x) ∈ V; rwa [hambient]⟩)
  have : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨f.fiberι s x, hmemU⟩⟩
  have : (I.ideal W).IsPrincipal := hprincipalW
  have hprincipal : (I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩).IsPrincipal := by
    rw [← I.map_ideal (V := W)
      (show (⟨U, hU⟩ : X.affineOpens) ≤ W from fun y hy => (hsubset hy).1)]
    infer_instance
  refine ⟨Spec Γ(X, U), hU.fromSpec, inferInstance, hU.range_fromSpec.symm ▸ hmemU, ?_⟩
  exact fiber_support_eq_union_affineChart f haffine I hgeneric s hdim hU hV hmemV
    (fun y hy => (hsubset hy).2) hprincipal

/-- **Stacks 053R.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a dominant morphism locally of finite type between
irreducible schemes, let `I` be a locally principal ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme
misses the generic fibre of `f`, and let `s` be a point of `S` whose fibre has dimension at most
that of the generic fibre. Then the support of the closed subscheme inside the fibre `X_s` is
set-theoretically the union of the irreducible components of `X_s` that it contains.

No Noetherian hypothesis: the Noetherian case
`Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents` is applied not to `f` but to a
finitely generated `ℤ`-algebra that the affine situation descends to, in
`Stacks.Divisors.fiber_preimage_zeroLocus_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents`. The two reductions in
front of that are
`Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents_of_isIntegral`, which passes to the
reductions of `X` and `S` and so makes both integral, and
`Stacks.Divisors.fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents_integral`, which localises to an
affine chart on which `I` is principal. -/
@[stacks 053R]
public theorem fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents_general {X S : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ S) [IrreducibleSpace S] [IrreducibleSpace X] [IsDominant f] [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (hI : IsLocallyPrincipal I)
    (hgeneric : IsEmpty ((I.subschemeι ≫ f).fiber (genericPoint S))) (s : S)
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber s) ≤ topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber (genericPoint S))) :
    (f.fiberι s) ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X) =
      ⋃₀ {C : Set (f.fiber s) | C ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber s) ∧
        C ⊆ (f.fiberι s) ⁻¹' (I.support : Set X)} := by
  refine fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents_of_isIntegral f ?_ I hI hgeneric s hdim
  intro X₀ S₀ f₀ _ _ _ _ I₀ hI₀ hgeneric₀ s₀ hdim₀
  refine fiber_support_eq_union_irreducibleComponents_integral f₀ ?_ I₀ hI₀ hgeneric₀ s₀ hdim₀
  intro A B _ _ _ _ _ _ _ g p hunit hdimA
  exact fiber_preimage_zeroLocus_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents g p hunit hdimA

end Stacks.Divisors

